----------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB SOURCE IS (parity scope)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
`withAiFeature.tsx` is a higher-order component, NOT a data/chart card. It folds
`useAiEnabled(feature)` and:
  • returns null unless the feature is on end-to-end (registry-known +
    settings resolved + ai_mode != off + ai_features[feature] === true);
  • when on, wraps the inner element in <div data-ai-feature data-testid>
    (data-testid = meta.uiTestIds[0] ?? `ai-feature-${feature}`);
  • throws at construction for an unknown feature id;
  • sets Wrapped.displayName = `withAiFeature(<id>, <inner>)`.
No charts, no maps, no user-facing copy (anonymous + transparent). The generic
template's loading/empty/error/stale/offline CHROME does NOT exist in this source
and is deliberately NOT invented (that would contradict the web `null`); instead
the full fail-closed gate truth table is modelled, every non-enabled verdict
rendering nothing (web null), per the AIChatbotIndicator gate precedent.

